{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109161","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109161/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109161/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109161/events","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109161","id":3280511985,"node_id":"I_kwDOAO6SJc7DiKPx","number":109161,"title":"Can't pass empty Dictionary/Array to a script's _init if it expects a typed Dictionary/Array, when instantiating from load()","user":{"login":"Lippanon","id":115422160,"node_id":"U_kgDOBuEz0A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/115422160?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon","html_url":"https://github.com/Lippanon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":279097162,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTcxNjI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/discussion","name":"discussion","color":"ccaaff","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098082,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwODI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gdscript","name":"topic:gdscript","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":12,"created_at":"2025-07-31T13:36:58Z","updated_at":"2025-07-31T17:34:28Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in: v4.4.1.stable.official [49a5bc7b6]\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 10\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using load() to load a script that has a typed Dictionary as an argument in its _init function, passing an empty Dictionary will fail with error:\n`Invalid type in function 'new' in base 'GDScript'. The dictionary of argument 1 (Dictionary) does not have the same element type as the expected typed dictionary argument.`\n\nSame thing with Array/typed Array.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nWith a simple class:\n```extends RefCounted\nclass_name SomeClass\n\nfunc _init(a_typed_dict: Dictionary[int, int]) -> void:\n\tprint(a_typed_dict)\n\tprint(\"is_typed: \", a_typed_dict.is_typed())\n```\n\nCalling the following code elsewhere will fail with error:\n`var _new_ref: SomeClass = load(\"res://some_class.gd\").new({}) # Fails`\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[bug-4.x.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21531536/bug-4.x.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109161/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109161/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}